      {
        "evidence_id": "E004",
        "passage_id": "P002",
        "quote": "The plaintiff commenced this action against the defendants, alleging that she fell when her foot became entangled in wires.",
        "statement_status": "allegation"
      },
      {
        "evidence_id": "E005",
        "passage_id": "P002",
        "quote": "The defendants failed to establish their prima facie entitlement to judgment as a matter of law dismissing the complaint insofar as asserted against Capo, as the evidence they submitted in support of their motion raised a triable issue of fact as to whether one of Capo's employees created the alleged hazardous condition ( see Willis v Galileo Cortlandt, LLC , 106 AD3d 730 , 732 [2013]; Velez v New York City Hous. Auth. , 91 AD3d 422 [2012]). Since the defendants failed to meet their prima facie burden as to Capo, that branch of their motion was properly denied without regard to the sufficiency of the plaintiff's opposition papers ( see Winegrad v New York Univ. Med. Ctr. , 64 NY2d 851, 853 [1985]).",
